{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And he brought the second ram, the ram of consecration, and Aaron and his sons laid their hands.</b> Now in the first occurrence it is written וסמך אהרן ובניו ('and Aaron and his sons laid [his hand]'). Yet there is no difference between וסמך אהרן ובניו and ויסמכו אהרן ובניו, for a great grammarian erred in saying that the meaning of וסמך is he alone, and afterward his sons, whereas ויסמכו means all of them together."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:09:04.153116722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}